From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 02:16:43 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 091/167] hjviewer: the update screens in the app's language
 (UX-W2)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

U35 (D3 (a), decided): every text of the update screens (P1-P7, B1, N1-N2,
C1a-U2, W1-W6, A1-A4, M1, I1-I3, E1-E4, O1) has an English side; an English
UI shows them in English, a Korean UI as before. The policy's own texts (its
notes and contact) show as the policy wrote them. The language follows the
window that asks: hjvEnabled() points HjvUpdateText at translate(), so a
session window's card for a PC below the minimum follows its UI too, and a
test without the core stays Korean. The deadline reads "November 23, 00:00"
in English. HjvUpdateText keeps its static switch (set from translate since
1.8.2 for About) rather than becoming an instance as the design sketched: the
same texts with no change at the call sites beyond dropping const.

D-1: where an update screen shows the policy's contact (whom to ask, the OS
that is too old, the move to Play), it reads "HJViewer 관리자: <contact>" /
"HJViewer administrator: <contact>", as About does; never a contact in the
app.

U43: a Windows PC that runs HJViewer without installing it hears, after
"다음부터는 새 파일(HJViewer-<latest>.exe)을 실행하세요.", "자주 쓰는 PC라면 새
버전에서 [설치하기]를 누르세요. 설치하면 다음부터는 저절로 업데이트됩니다." /
"If you use this PC often, press [Install] in the new version: once
installed, it updates by itself."

Tests: hjv_update_test.dart runs every screen, step and failure it knows on an
English UI (no Hangul, no braces, no link) and checks the English of the main
lines, U43 and the contact line; the gate test's contact line follows D-1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
